+
+## Infinite polar and qualitative argument
+
+The full chiral no-kernel result supplies kerB=kerB^T=0. Hence each bounded real B has an onto orthogonal polar factor even though its singular spectrum touches zero. The bare inverse columns used to exclude a kernel exist as l2 vectors, and the actual denominator1-2lambda/3 stays positive. The weighted inverses below are vectors in the appropriate spectral domains, not globally bounded inverses. The trace-class sign-projector path supplies S1-continuity of relative polar R-I.
