+Use the [endpoint](NATIVE_ZERO_PENALTY_ENDPOINT_NOTE_2026-09-08.md), [full dictionary](NATIVE_DYNAMICAL_CYCLE_FERMION_Z2_DICTIONARY_NOTE_2026-09-08.md) and [native algebra](NATIVE_EDGE_RECORD_MATTER_INSTRUMENT_AND_ENERGY_LEDGER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-05.md). Let every rectangular extent $L_a$ be even and at least four, $N=L_0L_1L_2$, and $t=g\lambda\ne0$ with uniform real coupling. Retain the full edge carrier and set $U=0$.
+
+The load-bearing external result is [Macris and Nachtergaele, Theorem 1.4](https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/9604043), with assumptions A1/A2, and its finite-temperature reflection remark. The proof below verifies its finite graph hypotheses and objective conversion. This is a mathematical import, not a numerical fit or an axiom-derived value. [Lieb's original theorem](https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9410025) supplies historical context, not a substitute for the stated applicability audit.
